  "body": "There are homes that impress from the street, and then there are homes that stop you in your tracks the moment the sun hits the cedar-clad façade. This is one of them. When golden light washes over the beautifully textured timber, this 504m² freehold residence, with a generous 327m² of interior space, becomes utterly unforgettable.\r\n\r\nStep inside, and you're greeted by a wall of floor-to-ceiling sliding glass that floods the open-plan living, dining, and kitchen areas with natural light. Slide them open, and the indoors melt seamlessly into a beautifully manicured, private backyard, level, secure, and waiting to host everything from summer gatherings with friends to after-school trampoline sessions and friendly basketball matches. It's also the kind of quiet sanctuary where you can simply breathe after a long day.\r\n\r\nBeyond the main living space, a separate lounge offers the perfect retreat, whether you envision a cozy home theatre for movie nights or an elegant sitting room for welcoming guests.\r\n\r\nFour oversized bedrooms provide ample space for the whole family, complemented by three well-appointed bathrooms. A massive double garage and an abundance of storage throughout mean every belonging has its place, making daily life feel effortlessly organised.\r\n\r\nBut it's the details that truly set this home apart. The owners have chosen every single light fixture with intention, the focused glow of the kitchen downlights, the sparkling elegance of the crystal chandelier in the living area, the romantic French-inspired pendant suspended above the bathtub. Together, they create a warmth that no photograph can quite capture, a feeling that says someone has loved living here, and you will too.\r\n\r\nAnd the location? It's the kind of address parents dream about. Zoned for Campbells Bay School, Murrays Bay Intermediate, and the prestigious double Westlake Colleges, your children's education is secured from start to finish.\r\n\r\nThis is more than a house. It's a home that has been curated, cared for, and now, lovingly released for its next family to fill with laughter.\r\n\r\nCome see it for yourself. Some homes speak to you. This one sings.",
